Our sg_split candidate "fixed_alt": the v1 series' fix alone — break the
sg_calculate_split() loop on nb_splits <= 0 (was !nb_splits), so the double
decrement cannot overshoot to -1.
Also the sg_split pin's PIN_PATCH (see sg_split.conf): the hunk applies
unchanged at 8b46fdaea819 and its parent.

Against lib/sg_split.c at v7.1 (same file as the v2 series base 08d0d3466664).
Made from the former vendored tests/irl/linux/sg_split/sg_split_fixed_alt.c; the
sg_split harness Makefile applies it (patch -o) to build that variant.

--- a/lib/sg_split.c
+++ b/lib/sg_split.c
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@
 			size = *(++sizes);
 		}
 
-		if (!nb_splits)
+		if (nb_splits <= 0)
 			break;
 	}
 
